r":[{"label":"This bill on Congress.gov","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/9432"}],"past":[]},"sponsor":{"chamber":"House","district":"7","id":"J000298","name":"Rep. Jayapal, Pramila","party":"D","state":"WA"},"stage":"in_committee","stage_label":"Referred to committee","summary":"The LIFT the BAR Act removes various restrictions on noncitizens regarding eligibility for federal public benefits. It repeals past limitations enacted under the Personal Responsibility and Work Opportunity Reconciliation Act of 1996 and Public Law 119-21, restoring access to programs such as Medicaid, the Children's Health Insurance Program, the Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program, and housing assistance for lawfully present noncitizens.","summary_detail":{"affected_groups":[{"effect":"Gain eligibility for various federal assistance programs including Medicaid, SNAP, housing assistance, and child nutrition programs.","group":"Lawfully present noncitizens"},{"effect":"Required to issue implementation guidance and alter program eligibility rules to comply with the removal of noncitizen restrictions.","group":"State and federal agencies"}],"key_provisions":["Repeals specific sections of the Personal Responsibility and Work Opportunity Reconciliation Act of 1996 and Public Law 119-21 that restrict noncitizen benefit eligibility.","Updates terminology throughout federal laws by replacing terms such as 'alien' and 'qualified alien' with 'noncitizen' and 'qualified noncitizen'.","Expands definitions of qualified noncitizens to include specific groups such as individuals with Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals, special immigrant juvenile status, and other federally authorized residents.","Prohibits states from denying child nutrition program benefits on the basis of citizenship or immigration status.","Restores premium tax credit allowances for certain lawfully present noncitizens."],"missing_information":["Exact estimates of the number of individuals who wo